This extension adds Alan Wake 2 modding support to Vortex Mod Manager.

This extension will automatically download and install the [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/alanwake2/mods/19]Alan Wake 2 Mod Loader[/url] during setup. This tool is needed to load loose file mods for the game.
Mods for the game can be downloaded from the [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/alanwake2/mods/]Alan Wake 2 Nexus site[/url].

[b]✅ Supported Versions:[/b]
[list]
[*]Epic[/*]
[*]Other versions may need to select the installation location manually.[/*]
[/list]
[b]🛠️ Mod Installation Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]Mod Loader installs to the game folder, recognised by a "version.dll" file.[/*]
[*]Game Data mods are recognised by a "data_pc" or "data" folder.[/*]
[/list]
[b]📋 Usage Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]You can open several useful files/folders/URLs using the buttons within the folder icon on the Mods toolbar.[/*]
[/list]

[b]📝 Notes for Mod Authors:[/b]
[spoiler]
Packaging rules for Alan Wake 2 mods, so Vortex installs them to the right place.

Vortex decides what a mod is by looking at the files and folders inside the archive. It tries each installer in order and the first one that matches wins, so archive layout is what determines where your mod ends up.

========================================================================

Mod Loader:

Recognised when the archive contains a "version.dll" file.

  Installs to: the game folder

========================================================================

Folders:

Recognised when the archive contains a "data_pc" or "data" folder.

========================================================================

Rules That Apply To Every Mod Type:

    - Folder and file name matching is case-insensitive.
    - Extra wrapper folders around a recognised folder are generally fine; the installer searches at any depth.
[/spoiler]

